@startuml
title UML - explicit preview review, atomic proof and post-commit response loss
actor Customer
boundary "Customer disclosure view" as UI
control "Customer BFF / API" as API
participant "Controls / native ownership" as Authority
participant "Documents native review" as Documents
participant "Core V1 material" as Core
database "Immutable review / requests / outbox" as DB
Customer -> UI : Read exact approved preview and check explicit review statement
UI -> API : POST exact disclosure digest + acknowledged=true\nOriginal Idempotency-Key / Origin / CSRF
API -> Authority : Authenticate current customer / canonical account owner
API -> Documents : Account + native policy + original actor/person/key/digest
Documents -> Documents : Lock issuer/subject/client/key then canonical person/account/policy
Documents -> Authority : Recheck and SHARE-lock current person link and active OWNER
alt First reviewed material
 Documents -> Core : Derive original native V1 material; verify policy integrity/product
 Core --> Documents : Exact full material
 Documents -> Documents : Require displayed digest; fixed statement and server UTC clock
 Documents -> DB : Atomically retain receipt + private attribution + request mapping + redacted event
else Exact retry or canonical alias
 Documents -> DB : Verify original immutable receipt / scope / private attribution
end
Documents --> API : Independently verified original receipt
API -> API : Validate full typed V1 proof before transaction commit
API --> UI : Response lost after native commit
UI -> API : Retry original key/body or GET own saved review
API -> Authority : Current owner still required
API -> DB : Verify exact retained record; no current-policy regeneration
DB --> UI : Same original receipt UUID / reviewed time / material / hashes
note over Customer,DB
PREVIEW_REVIEW_ONLY. No financial consent, enrollment, activation or posting.
Saved historical material does not certify current live policy validity.
end note
@enduml
